  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-based sea turtle conservation in Maio Island, Cape Verde: Increasing the sense of ownership in local communities to further reduce the poaching of females and nests on land and at sea.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recipient will; 1. conduct night patrols and count nests using standardized protocols on all major loggerhead nesting beaches on Maio; protect nests as necessary with a hatchery; 2. conduct educational and awareness program with local communuties on Maio; and 3. support a Guardians of the Sea progam that checks fishing boats for illegal fishing activities. The USFWS will work closely with grantee in setting goals, priorities, and developing budgets, and will provide assistance as needed and requested in engaging with National Governmental and other institutions to improve collaboration and conservation outcomes. USFWS will also provide assistance as necessary to ensure effective collaboration and cooperation between all MTCA grant recipients working within Cape Verde.</narrative>
  </description>
